el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas similares.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 122 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 24.8 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.9, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.8 to 6.4. December accounts for 74% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 29% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,286.10 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The high number of contracts just under the limit does not prove misconduct. It could reflect market pricing, budget constraints, or multiple needs. Statistical trends alone do not indicate improper actions by the body or awardees.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' dates and awardees to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Review the terms of contract [1] to ensure it aligns with the body's stated needs. Look for patterns in the number of contracts awarded to a single awardee.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["SiUb%2FDL%2BCQLyoM4us5k4vw%3D%3D","PCp9wpqxnzNSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","ise2KRTWcrIkJPJS%2BPS9vg%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}